# Deny-all, then re-include exactly what the backend image builds from.
#
# The blocklist version of this file sent a 188 MB context — `frontend/`
# (482 MB, mostly node_modules), `backend/target` (116 MB of build output) and
# `.git` (36 MB) are all in the repo root, and enumerating them is a losing
# game: every directory added later is included by default and nobody notices
# until a build is slow.
#
# Inverting it makes the context ~20 MB and, more usefully, makes it impossible
# for a new directory to leak in. The cost is that adding a genuinely needed
# path means adding a `!` line here — which is the right way round, because
# that failure is loud and immediate.
*

!backend/pom.xml
!backend/src

# Re-excluded inside the re-included paths: `backend/src` must never carry a
# stray target/ or node_modules from an experiment.
backend/**/target
backend/**/node_modules
**/.DS_Store
